From e3becc5cc0b22ee131726a20633cae58a94316ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Scott Sunarto <github@smsunarto.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 18:42:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] fix(source-control): draw blank context, read trimmed
 signatures and diff -r binary names (BBP-51 review 2)

A blank hunk line standing for context is drawn as that context line, so
Pierre's lines match the header counts. A + or - line after a finished hunk,
across blank lines or a signature, sends the file to text with a reason; a
signature without its trailing space still ends the mail. Binary lines split
in one pass and undo GNU's shell quoting; an unclear split reads as text.
Keys are path plus occurrence so they hold across re-reads; quoted paths no
longer overflow the stack; any parser failure returns a reason.
